    <!--
        THE BENCHES, one per stage of the lab's own SOPs.

        Names are the stage names the SOP and the floor already use, because the
        station board prints them and a technician has to recognise the one in
        front of them. The minutes per unit are NOT here: Odoo reads
        `time_start` as setup time and adds it to every work order on top of the
        operation's own duration, so the cycle from *Process Time Cycle* belongs
        to the operation in the bill of materials, where it is also allowed to
        differ from one product to the next.

        Cost per hour
        105.77 is the lab's own labour rate: 846.15 a day (their figure, used in
        every costing block) over an eight hour day. It reproduces their numbers
        exactly - model preparation at 60 units a day is 8 minutes a unit, and
        8 x 105.77 / 60 = 14.10, which is the figure in their sheet.

        A bench where nobody stands - a furnace, a printer, a curing unit -
        carries 0. That is not an omission: the lab's costing puts machine
        depreciation, power and compressed air in overheads, not in the hour
        rate, and inventing a machine rate would double-count them. The minutes
        are still recorded, so the schedule is right even where the cost is nil.

        A stage that exists in several departments is named for its department -
        "Acrylic Trimming", "Ortho Trimming" - because the department is what
        tells two otherwise identical benches apart.

        noupdate: the lab will re-time and re-rate these as it measures them,
        and an upgrade must not put this version back. (2026-09-25)
    -->
